# core: the host side of spill v2 and continued chats (port of GLM 0088, 0110 and 0111,
# MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold#78, #124 and #128), family-neutral: any native backend can bind
# them.
# - prompt_cache.zig: a Tier vtable the store calls on the engine thread only (lookup and counts in memory; restore
#   jobs begin/poll/cancel; keep, release, share, touch, flush), each call bounded; stale-aware find, probe, lineage
#   as a Fork chain on every entry, per-rank counters; Rules.grid/window for the native rule of where a point may sit
#   (on a chunk boundary, before the replay window). A restore replaces its point's memory twin when the family has
#   staled it (KV sharding's placements give a kept state's rows away): a lookup skips a stale state, so the restore is
#   the resume, not a drop and a recompute (found under pool stress on the pair: two 948K resumes recomputed with the
#   points on disk on both ranks, restores_dropped 2).
# - lane_host.zig: a request whose state is on disk is parked while the tier reads it beside decoding rounds
#   (TF_SPILL_LOAD_MS a round, 40; waits bounded by TF_SPILL_LOAD_WAIT_MS, 30000) and admitted once every rank holds
#   it; requests that want the same point share one restore; a clean stop gives the tier TF_SPILL_FLUSH_MS (60000) to
#   write what still waits.
# - 0111: a stream that continues its conversation without resuming that conversation's own kept state (a client
#   rewind, a state back from disk, states that were dropped) keeps the conversation instead of starting a new one,
#   so per-conversation room counts it once; /health and /metrics count chats_continued and
#   chats_continued_prefill_tokens.
# - server: --spill-dir, --spill-gib, --spill-min-free-gib, --spill-min-tokens, --spill-quota (TF_SPILL_TURNS, 4);
#   /health prompt_cache{..., spill{...}}, /metrics prompt_cache_* and spill_*{rank="N"}. A spill flag the backend
#   does not bind fails the open instead of being ignored.
# Everything is off by default: with no tier and no grouping the store and the host behave, count and report exactly
# as before (/health and /metrics byte-identical). Tests: lane_host_tier_test.zig and prompt_cache_tier_test.zig on an
# in-memory fake tier (prompt_cache_fake_tier.zig, one lock for the engine and test threads), and GLM's
# tools/chat_continued_check.py translated.
# The scheduler hooks follow BadAd84's block-tier design (MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold#118);
# GLM's 0111 builds on its 0089 kept states (Thomas Wade, PR #65), whose place the native prompt cache's conversations
# take here. By Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo). Apache-2.0.
